@page "/demo/layout"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-12: rebuilt on FeatureDemoLayout (was two framed demos and a static snippet). Two examples: an
   application shell (page layout + splitter, collapse buttons inside the demo) and the dashboard grid. Splitter added: the catalog already pointed here and no page rendered it. Facts checked
   against Layout/PageLayoutControl, Left/Center/RightPanelControl, DashboardLayoutControl, DashboardLayoutPanel
   and SplitterControl.razor in FlexCore 0.2.48. *@

<PageTitle>Page layouts — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Page layouts" Category="Components" ControlName="PageLayoutControl · SplitterControl · DashboardLayoutControl"
                   Tagline="An application shell with collapsible side panels and a splitter, and a dashboard grid."
                   SourcePath="Layout/PageLayoutControl.razor; SplitterControl.razor; Layout/DashboardLayoutControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            Three ways to divide a page. <code>PageLayoutControl</code> is a flex row of <code>LeftPanelControl</code>,
            <code>CenterPanelControl</code> and <code>RightPanelControl</code>; the side panels collapse to a 20px tab.
            <code>SplitterControl</code> puts a draggable bar between two panes, in pixels or as a share of the container,
            with keyboard resizing. <code>DashboardLayoutControl</code> is a CSS grid of panels placed by row, column and span; change those values and the grid re-flows.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="shell" Title="Application shell: panels and a splitter" RazorCode="@Code.Shell" CSharpCode="@Code.ShellCs">
            <Description><p><code>PageLayoutControl</code> rows up a navigation panel, the centre and a properties panel; each side panel collapses from its own tab or from the icon buttons in the centre, because <code>Collapsed</code> binds two ways. The centre holds a <code>SplitterControl</code>: drag the bar, or Tab to it and use the arrow keys, Home and End; double-click restores the first size. Bind <code>PrimarySize</code> two ways and persist from <code>OnResizeCommitted</code>, which fires once per gesture. The navigation, list and properties are wired together, so click around.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="frame">
                    <PageLayoutControl Height="340px">
                        <LeftPanelControl Width="170px" Collapsible="true" @bind-Collapsed="_leftCollapsed">
                            <div class="pane">
                                <h4>Navigation</h4>
                                <ul class="nav">
                                    @foreach (var sec in _data.Keys)
                                    {
                                        <li><ButtonControl BareStyle="true" CssClass="@($"nav-item {(sec == _section ? "active" : "")}")" OnClick="@(() => Go(sec))">@sec</ButtonControl></li>
                                    }
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </LeftPanelControl>
                        <CenterPanelControl>
                            <SplitterControl Height="100%" @bind-PrimarySize="_listSize" MinPrimary="140px" MaxPrimary="60%" MinSecondary="200px"
                                             OnResizeCommitted="@(_ => _commits++)" Title="Resize the list">
                                <PrimaryContent>
                                    <div class="pane">
                                        <h4>@_section</h4>
                                        <ul class="nav">
                                            @foreach (var it in _data[_section])
                                            {
                                                <li><ButtonControl BareStyle="true" CssClass="@($"nav-item {(it == _selected ? "active" : "")}")" OnClick="@(() => _selected = it)">@it.Title</ButtonControl></li>
                                            }
                                        </ul>
                                    </div>
                                </PrimaryContent>
                                <SecondaryContent>
                                    <div class="pane">
                                        @* Sidebar toggles the way editors do them: icon buttons, pressed while hidden, tooltip for the words. *@
                                        <div class="pane-head">
                                            <h4>@_selected.Title</h4>
                                            <div class="icon-row">
                                                <TooltipControl Text="@(_leftCollapsed ? "Show navigation" : "Hide navigation")" Placement="PopupPlacement.BottomEnd">
                                                    <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_leftCollapsed" IconCss="bi bi-layout-sidebar" aria-label="Toggle navigation" />
                                                </TooltipControl>
                                                <TooltipControl Text="@(_rightCollapsed ? "Show properties" : "Hide properties")" Placement="PopupPlacement.BottomEnd">
                                                    <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_rightCollapsed" IconCss="bi bi-layout-sidebar-reverse" aria-label="Toggle properties" />
                                                </TooltipControl>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <p>@_selected.Summary</p>
                                    </div>
                                </SecondaryContent>
                            </SplitterControl>
                        </CenterPanelControl>
                        <RightPanelControl Width="190px" Collapsible="true" @bind-Collapsed="_rightCollapsed">
                            <div class="pane">
                                <h4>Properties</h4>
                                <dl class="props">
                                    @foreach (var (key, value) in _selected.Props)
                                    {
                                        <dt>@key</dt><dd>@value</dd>
                                    }
                                </dl>
                            </div>
                        </RightPanelControl>
                    </PageLayoutControl>
                </div>
                <span class="result">List pane @_listSize.ToString("0") px, @_commits @(_commits == 1 ? "commit" : "commits") · navigation @(_leftCollapsed ? "hidden" : "shown"), properties @(_rightCollapsed ? "hidden" : "shown")</span>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="dashboard" Title="Dashboard grid" RazorCode="@Code.Dashboard" CSharpCode="@Code.DashboardCs">
            <Description><p><code>Columns</code> sets the grid; each panel takes <code>Row</code>, <code>Column</code>, <code>SizeX</code> and <code>SizeY</code>, here from page state. Click a KPI card to expand it across the row and back; hover one for its comparison. A panel is exactly its grid box, so spans are chosen to fit the cards. No script.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                @* .dash is the page-scoped ancestor that ::deep rules below need *@
                <div class="dash">
                <DashboardLayoutControl Columns="3" CellSpacing="@(new double[] { 12, 12 })" CellAspectRatio="0.35">
                    <DashboardLayoutPanels>
                        @foreach (var k in _kpis)
                        {
                            var t = _place[k.Key];
                            <DashboardLayoutPanel @key="k.Key" Row="t.Row" Column="t.Col" SizeX="t.SizeX" SizeY="t.SizeY">
                                <TooltipControl Text="@k.Detail" CssClass="tile-anchor" Placement="PopupPlacement.BottomStart">
                                    <div class="tile @(_focus == k.Key ? "focused" : "")" @onclick="() => Toggle(k.Key)" title="Click to expand">
                                        <CardControl Elevation="0" CssClass="dash-card"><ChartControl Type="ChartType.KpiCard" KpiValue="@k.Value" KpiLabel="@k.Label" KpiTrend="@k.Trend" Height="100px" /></CardControl>
                                    </div>
                                </TooltipControl>
                            </DashboardLayoutPanel>
                        }
                        <DashboardLayoutPanel Row="ChartsRow" Column="0" SizeX="2" SizeY="3">
                            <CardControl Elevation="0" CssClass="dash-card"><ChartControl Type="ChartType.Line" Title="Traffic" Height="200px" Series="_traffic" /></CardControl>
                        </DashboardLayoutPanel>
                        <DashboardLayoutPanel Row="ChartsRow" Column="2" SizeY="3">
                            <CardControl Elevation="0" CssClass="dash-card"><ChartControl Type="ChartType.Donut" Title="Sources" Height="200px" InnerRadius="0.5" Series="_sources" /></CardControl>
                        </DashboardLayoutPanel>
                    </DashboardLayoutPanels>
                </DashboardLayoutControl>
                </div>
                <span class="result">@(_focus is null ? "Three KPI cards on row 0, charts on rows 2–4." : $"{_kpis.First(k => k.Key == _focus).Label} spans the row; the others moved down.")</span>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="PageLayoutControl and panels" Rows="Vocab.PageLayout" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="SplitterControl" Rows="Vocab.Splitter" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="DashboardLayoutControl and DashboardLayoutPanel" Rows="Vocab.Dashboard" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables" Rows="Vocab.Vars" />
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>Panel collapse tabs are native buttons titled "Collapse panel" / "Expand panel"; their only text is an arrow glyph.</li>
            <li>The splitter bar is a native button with <code>role="separator"</code>, <code>aria-orientation</code> and the <code>Title</code> as its name. Arrow keys move it by <code>KeyboardStep</code>, Home and End go to the limits, double-click resets.</li>
            <li>The splitter imports the library's own <code>splitter-control.js</code> for the drag guide and measuring. No third-party script. Page layout and dashboard are CSS only.</li>
            <li>Dashboard panels are plain grid items with no landmarks or headings of their own; give each panel's content a heading.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Dockable, floating panes: <code>DockManagerControl</code> in the <a href="demo/counterparts?tab=docking">Control tour</a>. Tabbed MDI: <a href="demo/workspace/page-control-bench">PageControl</a>.</li>
            <li>Smaller helpers in the same namespace: <code>GridLayoutControl</code> (CSS grid with <code>Columns</code>, <code>Rows</code>, <code>Gap</code>, collapses on small screens) and <code>StackLayoutControl</code> (flex row or column with <code>Gap</code> and <code>Wrap</code>). The Control tour's forms use <code>GridLayoutControl</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

